## Why This Is Asked

Data provenance in multi-tenant analytics platforms is critical for compliance, cross-tenant data sharing, and debugging lineage issues. This question evaluates the ability to integrate Azure data cataloging services, OpenAI-powered analysis, and per-tenant security controls into a production-grade pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance and lineage tracking
- Microsoft Purview for metadata management
- Cognitive Search-powered versioned knowledge base
- Role-based access control (RBAC) with Azure Active Directory
- Data Lake auditing and logging
- Drift detection in ingestion pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lineage consistency validation
const validateLineage = (event) => {
  return event.source && event.sink && event.transactionId;
};

// Drift detection logic
const detectDrift = (expected, actual) => {
  return expected.source !== actual.source || 
         expected.sink !== actual.sink;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle real-time vs. batch lineage processing?
- What strategies would you use to minimize AI hallucinations when assessing lineage accuracy?
- How would you design the RBAC model to support nested tenant hierarchies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to stitch services: language detection, API routing, per-language OpenAI deployments, and privacy with session retention.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and multilingual routing
- API Management as gatekeeper and routing layer
- Language-specific OpenAI deployments and fallback
- Cosmos DB TTL for per-user context and PII handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample language detection using Azure Text Analytics
async function detectLanguage(text) {
  const client = new TextAnalyticsClient(endpoint, credential);
  const [result] = await client.detectLanguage([text]);
  return result.primaryLanguage.iso6391Name;
}

// prompt template with language context
const promptTemplate = (language, userMessage, context) => {
  return `You are a multilingual support assistant responding in ${language}. ` +
         `Previous context: ${context}\nUser: ${userMessage}\nAssistant:`;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a scalable, compliant code-scan assistant that maintains secret safety, leverages retrieval-augmented generation, and enforces per-tenant isolation using Azure services.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval augmented generation with Cognitive Search and a versioned KB
- Data privacy: redaction via Text Analytics and regex
- Per-tenant isolation: Cosmos DB + Key Vault
- Canary rollout and API Management integration
- Auditing to Data Lake and security controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline
async function scanDiff(diff, tenantId){
  const redacted = redact(diff, tenantId);
  const resp = callOpenAI(redacted, tenantKB(tenantId));
  logTelemetry(tenantId, diff.meta);
  return resp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate redaction coverage?
- How would you scale the KB and manage versioning across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of privacy safeguards in Azure OpenAI within multi-tenant SaaS, focusing on data leakage prevention, RBAC, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- PII detection and redaction pipelines
- Grounding with Cognitive Search over a versioned KB
- Per-tenant RBAC with Azure AD
- Data Lake auditing
- GDPR/CCPA compliance checks and synthetic-data tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redaction before OpenAI call
async function process(input, tenantId) {
  const pii = detectPII(input);
  const redacted = redact(input, pii);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, tenantId);
  return await openai.complete(prompt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify no PII leaks in logs or prompts across tenants?
- What metrics ensure latency remains acceptable under load?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design guardrails, multi-tenant routing, cost governance, and end-to-end Azure integration. It demonstrates knowledge of Durable Functions, API Management, Cognitive Search, Blob Storage, and Data Lake for audit logging and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation with per-tenant quota enforcement
- Pre- and post-processing guardrails for content safety
- Cost-aware routing with dynamic per-tenant budget allocation
- Versioned prompt templates stored in Blob Storage with Cognitive Search indexing
- Comprehensive auditing and observability via Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Guardrail function (illustrative)
async function checkGuardrails(prompt, tenantId) {
  const redacted = piiRedactor.redact(prompt);
  const lengthCheck = validateLength(redacted, MAX_TOKENS);
  const profanityCheck = profanityFilter.scan(redacted);
  return { redacted, lengthCheck, profanityCheck };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical Azure OpenAI engineering skills for data generation with governance, privacy, and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data policy gating
- PII redaction using Text Analytics
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and versioned KB
- Auditable logging to Data Lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-code: gate -> redact -> search -> openai
function handleInput(input, tenant) {
  if (!policyAllows(tenant, input)) throw new Error('Not allowed');
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const kb = searchKB(redacted, tenant);
  return callOpenAI(redacted, kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test PII redaction completeness?
- How would you manage KB versioning and cache invalidation?
